# The plural rules and plural ranges of CLDR release 49, for every locale it
# gives rules: what `plural_rules` reads, in the syntax `parse_plural_rules`
# reads, samples kept.
#
# The table is data, made and not typed: a one-off Heroes program,
# `gen_core.hero`, which is not in the tree (defect 2639), read CLDR 49's JSON
# (`cldr-49.0.0-json-full.zip` of
# https://github.com/unicode-org/cldr-json/releases, SHA-256 3b1f5d684d29c541,
# fetched 2026-11-18), its files `supplemental/plurals.json`, `ordinals.json`
# and `pluralRanges.json`, and wrote this module whole. Nothing here is edited
# by hand.

# The CLDR release the tables hold.
constant CLDR_VERSION: str
    "49"

